From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:42:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/m720q_m920q: Retrain memory for another CPU or HT
 setting

Reports on the M920q (coreboot.f4lc0n-industries.co.uk/m920q.html):
with a Hyper-Threading processor the memory training cache "may capture
invalid state" and then blocks the boots, with that processor and with
another one, until the BIOS region is written again; the workaround
there is to build without the cache. The cases have something in
common: the cache was made with Hyper-Threading the other way (the
CMOS default left it off, see below) or with another processor, and
FSP-M got it back.

Select FSP_PLATFORM_MEMORY_SETTINGS_VERSIONS and give the mainboard
bits of the cache version: bit 0 the "hyper_threading" option, bits 3:1
a hash of the processor's CPUID signature and brand string. Turning
Hyper-Threading on or off, or another processor, makes FSP-M train
again instead of resuming a cache made for another setup; a swap of
processors goes unseen once in eight. The first boot after this change
trains once, as the version of the cache changes.

cmos.default had no hyper_threading, so the CMOS option backend read 0
and the first boot ran with Hyper-Threading off on the processors that
have it, while the CFR one defaults to on: Enable, as the OEM firmware.

TEST=Built lenovo/m920x. On the M920x: one training after the update,
then the cache is used again; with Hyper-Threading turned off and on in
the setup, a training each time, in the hardware test.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig      |  1 +
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cmos.default |  1 +
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c   | 27 +++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig
index 159820afb2..c75234511a 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/Kconfig
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@ config BOARD_SPECIFIC_OPTIONS
 	select BOARD_ROMSIZE_KB_24576 if BOARD_LENOVO_M920Q || BOARD_LENOVO_M920X
 	select DRIVERS_OPTION_CFR_ENABLED if PAYLOAD_EDK2 && SMMSTORE
 	select DRIVERS_UART_8250IO
+	select FSP_PLATFORM_MEMORY_SETTINGS_VERSIONS
 	select HAVE_ACPI_RESUME
 	select HAVE_ACPI_TABLES
 	select HAVE_CMOS_DEFAULT
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cmos.default b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cmos.default
index f3330e5070..97cf35c794 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cmos.default
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/cmos.default
@@ -1,3 +1,4 @@
 boot_option=Fallback
 debug_level=Debug
 power_on_after_fail=Disable
+hyper_threading=Enable
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
index 51e7284034..d0ea9454c5 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
@@ -1,8 +1,10 @@
 /* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only */
 
+#include <arch/cpuid.h>
 #include <console/console.h>
 #include <device/pci_def.h>
 #include <device/pci_ops.h>
+#include <fsp/api.h>
 #include <mainboard/ec.h>
 #include <option.h>
 #include <soc/cnl_memcfg_init.h>
@@ -90,6 +92,31 @@ static uint8_t peg_enable(const FSPM_UPD *memupd)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The mainboard bits of the version of the memory training cache: a cache
+ * made with another processor, or with Hyper-Threading the other way, is
+ * not given back to FSP-M, which trains again. Bit 0 is the option, bits 3:1
+ * a hash of the processor's signature and brand string (a swap of processors
+ * goes unseen once in eight).
+ */
+uint8_t fsp_memory_mainboard_version(void)
+{
+	uint32_t hash = cpuid_eax(1);
+
+	for (uint32_t leaf = 0x80000002; leaf <= 0x80000004; leaf++) {
+		const struct cpuid_result r = cpuid(leaf);
+		hash = (hash ^ r.eax) * 0x01000193;
+		hash = (hash ^ r.ebx) * 0x01000193;
+		hash = (hash ^ r.ecx) * 0x01000193;
+		hash = (hash ^ r.edx) * 0x01000193;
+	}
+	hash ^= hash >> 16;
+	hash ^= hash >> 8;
+	hash ^= hash >> 4;
+
+	return (hash & 0xe) | !!get_uint_option("hyper_threading", CONFIG(FSP_HYPERTHREADING));
+}
+
 void mainboard_memory_init_params(FSPM_UPD *memupd)
 {
 	cannonlake_memcfg_init(&memupd->FspmConfig, &baseboard_mem_cfg);
-- 
